    tests: stage Founder policy and delivery inventory in Act 19 fixtures
    
    Both fixture towns invoke the real government/executive-cycle.sh, which
    requires government/AGENT-REPORTING-POLICY.md and reads
    government/delivery-candidates.py. They copied executive-cycle.sh without
    staging those two dependencies, so the suite failed with
    'Viche: mandatory Founder agent policy missing' before exercising anything.
    
    Staged dependencies only; no assertion is weakened or removed. Three fixture
    towns are affected: the main town and the 'safe' town in
    appointment-recovery-integration-smoke.sh, and Part 2's town in
    act19-office-continuity-smoke.sh.
    
    Before: tests/act19-office-continuity-smoke.sh exit 1.
    After:  both fixtures exit 0.

diff --git a/tests/act19-office-continuity-smoke.sh b/tests/act19-office-continuity-smoke.sh
index 0a2aaf33..aa1181e0 100644
--- a/tests/act19-office-continuity-smoke.sh
+++ b/tests/act19-office-continuity-smoke.sh
@@ -18,6 +18,11 @@ cp "$repo/government/eligible-work.py" "$d2/town/government/eligible-work.py"
 cp "$repo/government/executive-cycle.sh" "$d2/town/government/executive-cycle.sh"
 cp "$repo/government/handoff-queue.sh" "$d2/town/government/handoff-queue.sh"
 cp "$repo/government/predict-scorer.py" "$d2/town/government/predict-scorer.py"
+# The real executive-cycle.sh requires the Founder agent-reporting policy and
+# reads the delivery-candidate inventory. Stage both so the fixture exercises
+# the actual code path instead of failing on files it never copied.
+cp "$repo/government/AGENT-REPORTING-POLICY.md" "$d2/town/government/AGENT-REPORTING-POLICY.md"
+cp "$repo/government/delivery-candidates.py" "$d2/town/government/delivery-candidates.py"
